This embodiment serves multiple functions. For the rebellious audience, it shatters any comfortable distance between message and messenger. Ezekiel's body declares God's fury as much as his words do. For Ezekiel himself, he must feel in his own flesh the divine response to idolatry.\
The contrast with the mountains is notable. They passively hosted abominations; Ezekiel actively performs divine disgust at those abominations. The prophet's body becomes the opposite of corrupted sacred space - a human platform for displaying God's true response to false worship.\
Marshwiggle: That is what obedience looks like in this circumstance for Ezekiel, son of Adam who was made in the image of God.\
God's fury here is not limited to one part of the nation. Not just the city under threat of siege will fall to the sword. Those who escape that will die to plague. And those who escape that will die to famine. All God's wrath will be vented. Again, with the result that they will know he is the LORD.\
